{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-37685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{y}^{1}dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}[x]_{y}^{1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}(1-y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(\\frac{1}{1+{y}^{2}}-\\frac{y}{1+{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡y-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{2})}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡1-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{1}^{2})}{2}-(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{0}^{2})}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "632565cd94a2dea616a0f15e591eec21e084b75a6956ec5c82573c6560a8fd58"} {"question" "q-37685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-1"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}[x]_{0}^{{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}}{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{\\pi /2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}(0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37995" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "632565cd94a2dea616a0f15e591eec21e084b75a6956ec5c82573c6560a8fd58"} {"question" "q-37995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-37995" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-40581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curves $y=x-2,$ and $y=\\sqrt{x},$ above the $x$-axis. What is ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA\\,$ expressed as a repeated integral?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-40581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/6817e13f2f4c019f337425bd9f2284386c7077c0ac97da51fc26fdea19f8ee67.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=x-2$ and $y=\\sqrt{x}$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=x-2 & \\,⟹\\,x=y+2 \\\\ y=\\sqrt{x} & \\,⟹\\,x={y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =y+2 \\\\ {y}^{2}-y-2 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)(y+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/db9d1846b19b75a629ad0a0d4b6e138aa2cef91cd8c0324a9285ed9c44befb60.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le y+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-40581" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "632565cd94a2dea616a0f15e591eec21e084b75a6956ec5c82573c6560a8fd58"} {"question" "q-40581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-40581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{-y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y-2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{-y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy"] ["math" "{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-40581" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{y+2}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-y\\le x\\le 2y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,-y\\le x\\le 2y}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}[{\\int }_{-y}^{2y}x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{-y}^{2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}(2{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2})dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3{y}^{2}{e}^{{y}^{3}}\\,dy & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{{y}^{3}}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132529" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "632565cd94a2dea616a0f15e591eec21e084b75a6956ec5c82573c6560a8fd58"} {"question" "q-132529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{4}+2)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}+2)"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)"] ["math" "{e}^{4}-1"] ["math" "{e}^{8}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132529" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{8}-1)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/e15621dd6402a86de5c5d172880c7cbdc2a933e852259ad81d5ebcf9a89b9984.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}2x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10$ and $y=2x+1,$ above the line $y=1,$ as shown in the picture." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=10 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} \\\\ y=2x+1 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{2}(y-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y-1) \\\\ 2\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}} & =y-1 \\\\ (2\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}})^{2} & =(y-1)^{2} \\\\ 40-4{y}^{2} & ={y}^{2}-2y+1 \\\\ 5{y}^{2}-2y-39 & =0 \\\\ (5y+13)(y-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the line $y=1$, the $y$-limits are \n$1\\le y\\le 3.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/assets/33487fff6ff0b0e74bab4e6d6acdcb6902d40e938525d7de92d684ed5d98273a.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(y-1)\\le x\\le \\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}2x\\,dA={\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{\\int }_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}2x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}[{x}^{2}]_{(y-1)/2}^{\\sqrt{10-{y}^{2}}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}(10-{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}(y-1)^{2})dy & ={[10y-\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{12}(y-1)^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =(30-9-\\frac{2}{3})-(10-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{3}-\\frac{29}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "632565cd94a2dea616a0f15e591eec21e084b75a6956ec5c82573c6560a8fd58"} {"question" "q-132563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "11"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "\\frac{25}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{32}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{7}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"} {"question" "q-132563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{32}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068221/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bbb0dd9462973db1676ed8be5f9ffe12d7983bdccb93189904c8d48e3761a69"}] "usage" {"q-37995" []} "basis" 2298 "retractions" [[17592186134119 :question/problem "Calculate $∫_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{π/2}}∫_{0}^{y^{2}}\\sin y^{3}dxdy$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186131157 17592186131158 17592186131159 17592186131160 17592186131161] "immutable_fields" [[17592186131156 :answer-field/correct] [17592186131156 :answer-field/id] [17592186131156 :answer-field/key] [17592186131156 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
